">SCP-5819-B is to be kept in SCP-914’s containment area as a temporary containment cell until further notice.</span> SCP-5819-B is to be kept inside of Provisional Site-5819 for reasearch. SCP-5819-C doesn’t exist, so it doesn’t need to be, and can’t be, contained.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">SCP-5819 is a gold amulet, with a ruby<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-536856-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup> in the middle. When wearing SCP-5819, humans and gorillas begin to shrink until they’re so small, they’re invisible to the naked eye. When any other animal wears SCP-5819, they will grow until they either grow so big the ground beneath them can’t handle it’s mass and collapses or they die. SCP-5819 is observed to change size along with the subject until taken off. When SCP-5819 is took off a subject, the effect still remains.</span></p> <p>SCP-5819-A is the amulet itself. When held in a subject’s hand<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-536856-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >2</a></sup>, SCP-5819-A begins to shake vigorously. When took out of the subject’s hand, the effect remains for approximately a week. SCP-5819-B is the chain that let a subject wear SCP-5819 around their neck. When placed around the neck of a subject, the same effect as the former SCP-5819 occurs. SCP-5819-3 was the ruby in SCP-5819, see Incident-5819.</p> <p><strong>Incident-XXXX:</strong></p> <blockquote> <p>21:00 | 1st December, 2003<br /> The GOC broke into The Foundation. Tried to terminate a couple of SCPs. You know the drill.</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p>22:00 | 1st December, 2003<br /> I think one of ‘em saw SCP-5819. He said some things that I don’t remember exactly what he said. Something saying they found an SCP.</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p>23:00 | 1st December, 2003<br /> Two more of the GOC came. Don’t think any of ‘em saw me. If they did, they’d probably shot me by th